steps.prompt:
You are working in the daedalus-harness repo. The fixes phase just landed changes summarized here:

- fix-agent-mcp: {{steps.fix-agent-mcp.output}}

- fix-agent-compaction: {{steps.fix-agent-compaction.output}}

- fix-agent-tools: {{steps.fix-agent-tools.output}}

Write tests in agent/test/ that pin these fixes. Read the current code first (git diff HEAD in agent/src will show the recent fixes). Existing tests are in-process ACP clients over scripted MockLanguageModelV4s — see agent/test/helpers/scripted.ts and the existing test files for the harness pattern; follow it.

Cover at minimum: (1) an MCP tool call is gated by the permission system in always-ask mode and honors an always-allow answer; (2) re-loading a session closes/replaces the old MCP handle rather than leaking it (assert on close being called — a fake transport/client is fine); (3) compaction keeps the just-typed user prompt verbatim in session.messages and in the persisted JSONL; (4) a failing summarizer degrades to an uncompacted turn instead of failing it; (5) an empty summary does not replace history; (6) bash timeout kills the process group (spawn a shell that backgrounds a sleeping child; assert the grandchild dies) and pendingDelta stays bounded; (7) the grep fallback bails within its time budget on a pathological regex. Also add a pure unit test for globToRegExp in tools/search.ts.

You own agent/test/** only; do not modify agent/src — if a test reveals a fix is broken, report it in your final message instead of patching around it. Verify: cd agent && pnpm test. Summarize what you covered and anything you found broken.

You are the final gate of a 15-step remediation workflow on the daedalus-harness repo. Every earlier step has landed; their reports:

FIXES — mcp: {{steps.fix-agent-mcp.output}} | compaction: {{steps.fix-agent-compaction.output}} | tools: {{steps.fix-agent-tools.output}}
HARDENING: {{steps.harden-server.output}}
TESTS — agent: {{steps.agent-tests.output}} | server: {{steps.server-tests.output}}
REFACTOR — server: {{steps.refactor-server.output}} | actions: {{steps.refactor-client-actions.output}} | thread-items: {{steps.refactor-thread-items.output}} | local-stores: {{steps.refactor-local-stores.output}} | dedup: {{steps.refactor-client-dedup.output}}
OPTIMIZE — store: {{steps.optimize-store-selector.output}} | workspace-fs: {{steps.optimize-workspace-fs.output}} | persistence: {{steps.optimize-agent-persistence.output}}
CLEANUP: {{steps.cleanup-wiring.output}}

Run the full verification sweep: (1) cd client && pnpm exec tsc -b; (2) cd server && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit && pnpm test — plus pnpm test:gateway, test:workflow-schema, test:workflow, test:quota, test:backup if those scripts exist; (3) cd agent && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit && pnpm test. Fix only trivial integration breakage between workstreams (a moved import, a renamed export); anything substantive gets reported, not patched around. Then read git status and git diff --stat for a sanity pass: no step should have left debris (stray files, console.logs, commented-out code). Do NOT commit anything — the user reviews and commits.

Your final message is the run's report: overall pass/fail per suite, what you had to repair, anything a step reported as broken or incomplete, and a short list of what a human should review most carefully.
